{
  "name": "Chat with your Google Drive documents using Gemini and a free in-memory vector store",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Chat with your Google Drive documents using Gemini and a free in-memory vector store\n\nAsk questions about the PDFs, Google Docs and text files in one Google Drive folder and get answers that name the files they came from. No Pinecone, Supabase or other paid vector database: documents are embedded with Gemini's free embedding model and kept in n8n's built-in in-memory vector store.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Index my documents** (click to run, plus a daily schedule) lists the folder, keeps supported files and downloads them (Google Docs are exported as text).\n2. **Store in the in-memory vector store** splits each file into chunks, embeds them with Gemini and stores them with the file name and link.\n3. **When a chat message is received** opens n8n's hosted chat. **Answer from the documents** (AI Agent + Gemini) searches the store and answers only from what it finds, naming the source files.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add **Google Drive OAuth2** and **Google Gemini (PaLM) API** credentials (free key at aistudio.google.com).\n2. Put your folder ID (the last part of the folder URL) in **Set index settings**.\n3. Run **Index my documents** once, then activate the workflow and open the chat URL from the chat trigger.\n\n### Good to know\nThe in-memory store is cleared when n8n restarts; the daily schedule rebuilds it. For a persistent index, Telegram access, cited passages and an unanswered-questions digest, see the Pro version.\n\nFailure alerts: fill in the alert node in **Alert on errors** and choose this workflow under **Settings > Error workflow**.",
        "height": 1040,
        "width": 600
      },
      "id": "1d6c2318-f4f2-50be-a1d1-b2169b2014b6",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -420
      ]
    },
